    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Application—insertion of section 44ZZMAA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017#sch-1-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendment made by Part 1 of this Schedule to insert\nsection 44ZZMAA of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 applies\nin relation to a decision made before, on or after the commencement of\nthis Schedule, subject to subitem (2).\n(2)\nThe amendment does not apply in relation to a decision if an application\nfor merits review of the decision by the Tribunal was made before",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendment made by Part 1 of this Schedule to insert\nsection 44ZZMAA of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 applies\nin relation to a decision made before, on or after the commencement of\nthis Schedule, subject to subitem (2).\n(2)\nThe amendment does not apply in relation to a decision if an application\nfor merits review of the decision by the Tribunal was made before",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-6-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "263a133ec1225ea07610475a9096d61c1124a5fa40e11196e978d04f8b28f924",
      "skos:note": "Amendment applies in relation to decisions made before, on or after commencement, subject to subitem (2)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017#sch-1-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Application—insertion of section 44ZZMAA",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendment made by Part 1 of this Schedule to insert\nsection 44ZZMAA of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 applies\nin relation to a decision made before, on or after the commencement of\nthis Schedule, subject to subitem (2).\n(2)\nThe amendment does not apply in relation to a decision if an application\nfor merits review of the decision by the Tribunal was made before"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-6"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-6-logic-alleninterval-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal relation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 June 2017.",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017#sch-1-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(3)\nHowever, subitem (2) does not prevent the amendment applying in\nrelation to a decision covered by subsection 44ZZMAA(1) of that Act\n(as inserted by this Act) if the decision is made on the remittal of a\nmatter by the Tribunal.\nNote:\nA matter may be remitted by the Tribunal following merits review by the Tribunal of\nsuch a decision if an application for merits review was made before 21 June 2017.\nSubitem (3) prevents an application for merits review by the Tribunal of the decision on\nthe remitted matter.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 10 August 2017\nSenate on 5 September 2017]\n\n(158/17)",
      "skos:definition": "(3)\nHowever, subitem (2) does not prevent the amendment applying in\nrelation to a decision covered by subsection 44ZZMAA(1) of that Act\n(as inserted by this Act) if the decision is made on the remittal of a\nmatter by the Tribunal.\nNote:\nA matter may be remitted by the Tribunal following merits review by the Tribunal of\nsuch a decision if an application for merits review was made before 21 June 2017.\nSubitem (3) prevents an application for merits review by the Tribunal of the decision on\nthe remitted matter.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 10 August 2017\nSenate on 5 September 2017]\n\n(158/17)",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-21-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-21-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-21-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-21-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-21-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-21-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cfce6c0e64c60c414db5fd72c228e53a0efb456f96d431b1d6df1ad47bfbbb8e",
      "skos:note": "Prevents an application for merits review by the Tribunal of the decision on the remitted matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017#sch-1-sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 June 2017.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(3)\nHowever, subitem (2) does not prevent the amendment applying in\nrelation to a decision covered by subsection 44ZZMAA(1) of that Act\n(as inserted by this Act) if the decision is made on the remittal of a\nmatter by the Tribunal.\nNote:\nA matter may be remitted by the Tribunal following merits review by the Tribunal of\nsuch a decision if an application for merits review was made before 21 June 2017.\nSubitem (3) prevents an application for merits review by the Tribunal of the decision on\nthe remitted matter.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 10 August 2017\nSenate on 5 September 2017]\n\n(158/17)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-abolition-of-limited-merits-review-act-2017-sch-1-sec-21-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
